{"name":"Petroleum","hex":"#21211d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Petroleum","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A place in the United States:\nAn unincorporated community in Nottingham Township, Wells County, Indiana.\nAn unincorporated community in Allen County, Kentucky.\nAn unincorporated community in Ritchie County, West Virginia.","An unincorporated community in Nottingham Township, Wells County, Indiana."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Petroleum"}],"entries":[{"title":"Petroleum","blocks":[{"text":"Petroleum, also known as crude oil or simply oil, is a natural resource that appears as a yellowish-black liquid chemical mixture found in geological formations, consisting primarily of hydrocarbons. The term petroleum refers to both naturally occurring unprocessed crude oil, as well as to petroleum products that consist of refined crude oil."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Petroleum_sample.jpg/330px-Petroleum_sample.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Petroleum","wikidata":"Q22656"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Oil_well.jpg/500px-Oil_well.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Oil_well.jpg/500px-Oil_well.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOil_well.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Photo_lg_kuwait.jpg/500px-Photo_lg_kuwait.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Photo_lg_kuwait.jpg/500px-Photo_lg_kuwait.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APhoto_lg_kuwait.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/Treibs%26Chlorophyll.png/500px-Treibs%26Chlorophyll.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/Treibs%26Chlorophyll.png/1280px-Treibs%26Chlorophyll.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/Treibs%26Chlorophyll.png/500px-Treibs%26Chlorophyll.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The close structural similarity of vanadium porphyrin compound (left) extracted from petroleum and chlorophyll a (right) established the biological origin of petroleum.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATreibs%26Chlorophyll.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Gusher_Okemah_OK_1922.jpg/500px-Gusher_Okemah_OK_1922.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Gusher_Okemah_OK_1922.jpg/500px-Gusher_Okemah_OK_1922.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An oil derrick in Okemah, Oklahoma in 1922","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGusher_Okemah_OK_1922.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Ignacy_Lukasiewicz.jpg/330px-Ignacy_Lukasiewicz.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Ignacy_Lukasiewicz.jpg/330px-Ignacy_Lukasiewicz.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Ignacy Łukasiewicz, credited with the first commercial oil extraction in 1854 in Bóbrka, Poland, and opening the world's first industrial oil refinery","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AIgnacy_Lukasiewicz.jpg"},{"srcset